  "name": null,
  "problem": "A farm sells its apples to three grocery stores; $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$\n\n- Store $1$ buys $14%$ of the apples.\n\n- Store $2$ buys $26%$ of the apples, and $50%$ of those apples are sold in one day.\n\n- Store $3$ buys $60%$ of the apples, and $25%$ of those apples are sold in one day.\n\nIf $63%$ of all apples are red, $25%$ of red apples are sold in one day, and $45%$ of apples sold in one day are red, what is the probability that a randomly chosen apple bought by store $1$ is sold in one day? Round your answer to $1$ decimal place.",
